# Maps source markdown (theme / sub-area) to GitHub issue. Tab-separated.
# Format: <markdown-path>\t<owner/repo>\t<issue-number>
# Lines starting with '#' are comments.
#
# This file is an EXAMPLE. The actual mapping (scripts/epic-issue-map.tsv) is
# operator-local and gitignored, because the issue numbers depend on which
# repo the operator is seeding against and they are not part of the canonical
# spec corpus.
#
# Workflow for the operator:
#   1. cp scripts/epic-issue-map.tsv.example scripts/epic-issue-map.tsv
#   2. Edit scripts/epic-issue-map.tsv and fill in the real issue numbers in
#      the third column. The placeholder is `0` — replace it with the issue
#      number from `gh issue view <N>` once each issue exists in the target
#      repo.
#   3. Run scripts/sync-epic-to-issue.py against your local manifest. The
#      example file is never read by the script.
#
# Theme entries come first in each block; sub-area (epic) entries follow.

